INV-zuhig, the last blocker before INV-dabuf's rc 3 can be claimed on
evidence. Two halves, one per layer:

LINKER. argparse registers subcommand handlers via
`parser.set_defaults(func=handler)` and dispatches them at runtime with
`args.func(args)`. The analyzer records the registration as a
`references` edge — structurally honest, but it leaves every
argparse-dispatched handler with no call-shaped edge from production
structure, so a `start_at: callee` taint source on such a handler can
never mint a flow. The new Framework linker `argparse_dispatch` emits
`dispatches_to` edges from the registration site's enclosing function to
the resolved handler, following go_cobra's conventions: two-anchor
pre-filter (`.set_defaults(` + an `argparse` mention), paren-balanced
multi-line argument spans, ANY kwarg name (unlike cobra's fixed field
set, argparse's set_defaults key is user convention — func/handler/cls
all appear in the wild), identifier values only (literals, lambdas and
call expressions skipped), callable-kind resolution filter
(function/method/class), 0.5-confidence disambiguation fallback on
short-name collisions. On hypergumbo's own cli.py the pattern recovers
all 26 cmd_* registrations with zero non-func noise.

TAINT. `dispatches_to` joins TAINT_CALL_EDGE_TYPES. This is the CLASS
fix: every Framework dispatch linker (cobra, decorator, django, jackson,
kafka, caddy, airflow, rust-trait — and now argparse) emits
`dispatches_to` for "runtime dispatch will invoke dst with data src
controls", and taint was blind to the entire family — sources behind a
dispatch boundary never minted, and BFS never crossed one. Membership is
monotone-additive for adjacency and minting; the one non-additive
surface (sanitizer registration over dispatch edges) deliberately shares
the same predicate — one rule, one home — and cannot fire on this repo
(dispatch dsts here are cmd_* handlers, never sanitizers).

Why Go's analyzer hid this for cobra: it records `RunE: runServe` in an
instance-form composite literal as a `calls` edge, so instance-form
cobra handlers minted all along. The dominant package-level
`var rootCmd = &cobra.Command{...}` idiom emits NO analyzer call edge —
there the linker's dispatch edge is now the only minting route, same as
Python.

