  self-proof (python/argparse):
    rc                          3 (unchanged)
    verdicts                    18/18 confirmed_with_caveats (unchanged)
    sanitizer-credited flows    0 -> 98   <- the evidence INV-dabuf needs
    total examined flows        295 -> 1,007
    (structural 28 -> 12 is a path-relabel into ddg_mixed on the larger
    graph, not a deletion: +728 ddg_mixed = 712 new + 16 relabeled, ddg
    count byte-stable at 16, and no violation existed before or after)

  cobra fixture (go, package-level var idiom):
    registered handler          claim VIOLATED — source minted through
                                the dispatches_to edge, the only
                                call-shaped edge into it
    identical orphan handler    inconclusive (opaque launch), NOT
                                violated — no registration, no minting
                                (negative control)

Attribution on the self-proof is by construction: runtime_cli_entry can
only mint at cmd_* handlers, tests are outside the artifact scope, and
the only in-artifact call-shaped edges into cmd_* are the linker's —
the same tree without this change measured 0 credited flows on all 18
verdicts.

Boundary pinned by test: a raw `references` edge still does NOT mint.
The registration reference is not evidence the handler runs; only the
linker's call-shaped edge is.

